Name: realtek-8111 (Realtek RTL8111/8168/8411 ethernet driver)
License: BSD-style (see per-file Fuchsia copyright headers)
Upstream: https://fuchsia.googlesource.com/fuchsia
Upstream path: src/connectivity/ethernet/drivers/realtek-8111
Revision: 0f3c21bc
Fetched via: gitiles +archive
  https://fuchsia.googlesource.com/fuchsia/+archive/0f3c21bc/src/connectivity/ethernet/drivers/realtek-8111.tar.gz

Vendored-at-baseline into Cerise. Files taken verbatim from upstream @ 0f3c21bc:
  rtl8111.cc, rtl8111.h, meta/realtek-8111-info.json, meta/bind-tests.json

Files adapted for Cerise (see in-file comments for the exact divergences):
  meta/realtek_rtl8111.bind  - composite bind adapted to the node spec bus-pci
                               publishes in this tree (mirrors e1000.bind; drops the
                               upstream BIND_PCI_INTERFACE==1 constraint; requires the
                               acpi parent with ACPI_BUS_TYPE==PCI).
  meta/realtek-8111.cml      - shard-include style matching Cerise's compiled_manifest
                               (identical to upstream in substance; DFv1/compat shape).
  BUILD.bazel                - authored for Cerise (Bazel). Upstream BUILD.gn kept for
                               reference below is NOT used.
  realtek-8111.ld            - version script (exports only the two ZIRCON_DRIVER
                               registration symbols), authored for Cerise, modeled on
                               platform-bus-x86.ld.

DRIVER SHAPE: DFv1 / legacy. It uses the banjo EthernetImpl/EthernetIfc protocol
(fuchsia.hardware.ethernet, vendored alongside at
src/upstream/fuchsia/sdk/banjo/fuchsia.hardware.ethernet), ddktl (ddk::Device),
io-buffer, and registers via ZIRCON_DRIVER. It rides the compat shim (compat.so) —
program.compat = "driver/realtek-8111.so" — exactly like platform-bus-x86 and bus-pci.
It is NOT DFv2 (no fdf::DriverBase, no __fuchsia_driver_registration__).

BUILD-ONLY: QEMU cannot emulate RTL8111, so this driver is build-verified only. It is
intended to first run on a real Apollo Lake NUC whose NIC is a Realtek RTL8111HN
(PCI 10ec:8168 family).

Upstream note (from rtl8111.h): "This driver has only been tested on the 8111h rev2
(0x54100000), but it should work (or mostly work) with any model of rtl8111, rtl8168,
or rtl8411." And (from rtl8111.cc): "This driver has not been tested since rewriting in
C++."
